-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Head Over Heels
  Publisher   Ocean, 1987
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Head over Heels (1987)(Ocean)(128K)[aka Foot and Mouth].z80
  MD5         757bbabf443a643cbe376ebfb11baa79

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

  Memory      Any Next: a 1MB Next has the memory for the game. Enhanced needs
              a 1MB Next, and is not offered on a smaller one.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  The game's play area has no colour clash, so none is removed: the default
  keeps the original look. The patch adds the menu, its cheats and the Next
  start-up. The menu's Next presentation line adds more; see the note. Game
  logic is unchanged. Enhanced colours, an option on the menu, are below.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    Anthony Lycett's colours: Head and Heels in their own colours,
              red and blue brick walls, chequered floors, gold doors and
              coloured panel icons; the game's printed text keeps its original
              look. Source: Enhanced colours: Anthony Lycett (Spec256).

  Pace        original

  Note        Keys: the game's own menu sets keys or joystick; Head and Heels
              swap, join and use items as in the original. The 128K release
              with its AY music and the original loading screen. Default keeps
              the original monochrome look: the play area has no colour clash
              to remove. Enhanced paints the figures, rooms, doors, floors and
              panel icons in Anthony Lycett's Spec256 colours; off by default.
              Fits a 1MB Next. Known issues: channel C sound effects can start
              on a different interrupt phase than the original after faster
              drawing; music channels A and B match. In JNext pace is within
              0.02 percent in quiet scenes and up to 0.41 percent faster in
              busy ones, slowest 20-update stretch +0.02 percent. Missing:
              natural play to the end and every room; hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Immunity
   3  Infinite ammo/specials
   4  Springy jumps
   5  Mega jumps
   6  Respawn special items
   7  Keep hush puppies
   8  All items + 99 shots

  Archive Head Over Heels POK. Use the verified alternate infinite-lives
  address 42195; first lives entry still decrements. Starter equipment/ammo
  translated to new-game templates 41602/41609 because archive runtime
  addresses are reset. Overlapping starter variants consolidated into all
  items and 99 shots.

